course: dictionary
lesson: 15735
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word transmission is a good example. «Washing your hands stops the transmission of germs.» Here transmission means passing something from one person to another, so germs are being passed on.
explain: «The live transmission of the football match started at three o'clock.» Here transmission means a programme sent out by radio or TV. The clues are live and match, not the word itself.
explain: «The transmission in our car broke, so the mechanic had to fix the gearbox.» Here transmission means the part of a vehicle that sends power from the engine to the wheels. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Transmission means the passing of something from one person, place or thing to another.
fact: Transmission can also mean sending out radio, TV or electronic signals, or the programme or message that is sent.
fact: In a vehicle, the transmission is the part that sends power from the engine to the wheels. It is also called the gearbox.
fact: A car's transmission can be manual or automatic.
exercise: «Washing your hands stops the transmission of germs.» What does transmission mean here? | Washing with soap and water | *Passing germs from one person to another | The gearbox in a car | A live programme on TV
exercise: «The live transmission of the concert was seen by millions.» What does transmission mean here? | Passing a message to a friend | *A programme or signal sent out by TV or radio | The part of a car that moves the wheels
exercise: «The mechanic checked the transmission before the long drive.» What does transmission mean here? | A message sent by a phone | Passing a cold on to a friend | *The gearbox, the part that sends power from the engine to the wheels
test: «Signals travel by transmission through cables, radio waves or satellites.» What does transmission mean here? | The part of a car that sends power to the wheels | *Sending signals through cables, radio waves or satellites | Washing hands with soap
test: Which sentence uses transmission to mean a broadcast that was stopped? | «The transmission of power to the wheels was smooth.» | *«The transmission was interrupted, so the news stopped.» | «The transmission of the cold spread through the class.»
exam: Ella reads «In an automatic transmission, the car changes gear by itself.» What does transmission mean here? | A live programme on TV | Passing germs from one person to another | Sending a message to a friend | *The gearbox, which sends power from the engine to the wheels
